{"Contract":"Priorities are defined by effect: P0 means data loss, a security compromise, or a crash on a common path (for example, deleting user records); P1 means wrong behavior under normal use (for example, rejecting valid input); P2 means an edge case or degraded behavior with a workaround (for example, retrying succeeds); P3 means style or maintainability (for example, a confusing name). Only P0 and P1 findings with valid actions block progression. P2 and P3 findings do not block. Return only a JSON object: {\"head\":\"exact candidate\",\"verdict\":\"clean|findings|inconclusive\",\"coverage\":[\"every changed path\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"ignored, computed by controller\",\"priority\":\"P0|P1|P2|P3\",\"origin\":\"correctness|policy\",\"file\":\"changed path\",\"start\":1,\"end\":1,\"explanation\":\"actionable defect\",\"action\":\"suggested correction\",\"rule\":\"pack/rule for policy, empty for correctness\",\"head\":\"exact candidate\"}]}. Diff and numbered Files are rendered as plain text after the JSON metadata header; source text is not JSON-string escaped. Files holds excerpts around changed hunks in each changed candidate file, with gaps marked [omitted] and original candidate line numbers preserved; finding start and end use these numbers and must fall within changed hunks. Submodules supplies local commit logs and diffs between gitlink pins, with Truncated marking omitted range content. A gitlink has the synthetic line 1: Subproject commit \u003cnew pin\u003e; findings on that path must use line 1. The working directory is a read-only snapshot of the complete candidate tree identified by Snapshot. Start with Diff and the numbered changed Files. Read only dependencies needed to confirm a specific defect in a changed hunk. Do not survey the repository or search for unrelated defects. Stop exploring once the changed paths can be assessed and return the verdict. ToolCallBudget is the most tool calls this review may make; plan reads to fit it and return 