+With `review_provider = "greenhouse"`, `full-pipeline` uses the Greenhouse prepublication handoff instead of private candidates and `posse validate`: the Worker commits and signals `done --head <sha>` without publishing. The Task Signal binds the requested head. Project maintenance, outside the Task cgroup, requests the Greenhouse Verdict. A current passing Verdict queues the Worker to publish that exact head; `posse publish` refuses any head without its own passing Verdict. A moved head voids the request and needs a new done Signal. Blocking findings are stored in the provider-neutral Finding Ledger, then selected and resolved through the existing Review Fix Round flow; inconclusive results block publication without queueing a fix. No Review Task is created. `quick` keeps its merge-time Greenhouse gate and existing publication flow. Legacy Tasks with no frozen provider follow the current Project provider, while their earlier built-in Review rounds remain readable and count toward the frozen cap.
