1256: #### none and quick flow
1257: 
1258: After a loop-enabled Change signals done, preserve the existing path: freshness -> selected review -> pinned Merge, with PR-watch CI allowed in parallel with review on the published head. When `review_loop.profile` is unset and dispatch resolves no single Profile, auto-start considers only the Profiles of unconditional `type = "review"` rules whose launch starts a fresh session. Exactly one such Profile is used; config order never breaks a tie. It never chooses a conditional candidate, an untyped rule or `dispatch.default.use` from a `profile_required` list. With no unconditional review candidate, or with several distinct eligible Profiles, it raises the readiness Notice, which names the candidates and asks for `review_loop.profile`. `posse review start` without `--profile` follows the same rule and fails with `profile_required`. `posse doctor` warns when Review auto-start is enabled and would raise that Notice. Missing reviewer resolution produces one readiness Notice per head naming each candidate and why it was rejected, but never satisfies required `quick` evidence; explicit start reports the session/Profile error. `none` does not acquire a fictitious review pass. Known blocking findings remain blocking under either mode.
1259: 
1260: #### full-pipeline flow
1261: 
1262: With `review_provider = "greenhouse"`, `full-pipeline` uses the Greenhouse prepublication handoff instead of private candidates and `posse validate`: the Worker commits and signals `done --head <sha>` without publishing. The Task Signal binds the requested head. Project maintenance, outside the Task cgroup, requests the Greenhouse Verdict. A current passing Verdict queues the Worker to publish that exact head; `posse publish` refuses any head without its own passing Verdict. A moved head voids the request and needs a new done Signal. Blocking findings are stored in the provider-neutral Finding Ledger, then selected and resolved through the existing Review Fix Round flow; inconclusive results block publication without queueing a fix. No Review Task is created. `quick` keeps its merge-time Greenhouse gate and existing publication flow. Legacy Tasks with no frozen provider follow the current Project provider, while their earlier built-in Review rounds remain readable and count toward the frozen cap.
1263: 
1264: 1. **Private candidate custody and freshness (VP-B).** For `full-pipeline`, `posse publish` is the submission entry point. It requires the existing clean, committed Task-branch preconditions, records submitted head `S`, frozen target tip `T`, and expected remote Task-branch head, then creates a durable private candidate ref and checkout without pushing or opening a PR. `none` and `quick` keep the existing publish behavior. The validation lane exclusively owns candidate head `H`; a later publish or Signal that finds the author branch moved refuses with both heads and requires resubmission for a fresh candidate. A stale candidate does not report `candidate_author_moved` when its Task branch still equals submitted head `S`. Before publish refreshes a stale candidate, it refuses and lists any Review fix commits that remain only in `H`; merge those commits into the Task branch first. To drop a newer candidate instead, for example after the User reverts a scope change, reset the Task branch to the previously promoted head (origin must still be there) and run `posse candidate abandon <task> [--repo <member>] --reason <why>`: Posse moves the candidate to its archive ref, marks it and any unpromoted candidates since the promotion `discarded`, restores the promoted candidate, and records the abandonment in Task history. A done Signal then succeeds without a republish. While a candidate is pending, neither promoted nor abandoned, `posse merge` and `posse merge --execute` refuse with `candidate_pending`, naming both heads, and no `merge_ready` is raised; `merge_ready` and Merge output name the head they merge. Persisted refs and records let Posse recover the candidate checkout after a crash. Candidate submission fetches the frozen target and merges it into the private candidate when needed (ADR 0019), never rebasing a published lineage. No new daemon or local bare repository is required. The candidate checkout is a fresh worktree. Set `pipeline.candidate_files = ["app.yaml"]` in the Project config to copy listed repository-relative gitignored files from the Sandbox before validation. A workspace Member can override the list with `repositories.<member>.candidate_files`. Entries are plain paths without globbing. Posse reports listed files missing from the Sandbox and continues submission. The `worker-home-write` guard allows the copy only into this Worker's own Task candidate. Gitignored files do not count as candidate changes: they never block validation or promotion and are never published.
1265: 2. **Review.** An independent identity-eligible Reviewer examines `H` through the numbered/delta Review Loop. Missing Profile, failed or inconclusive review blocks. Review fixes are author changes in the candidate lane, not permission to publish; the lifetime cap does not reset for any repair source. When a numbered Review Round passes while the Change Task is `done` and every full-pipeline target is still its active reviewed candidate, Posse queues the Worker, in the transaction that records the verdict, to run test -> docs -> lint in each candidate checkout and promote it, and raises `candidate_validation_queued`; the Lead sends nothing.
1266: 3. **Test (intent proof).** Prove the Brief's intended behavior, using end-user/E2E evidence where applicable, and record commands, results and artifacts. Deterministic test results complement, not replace, intent proof. Inconclusive evidence is not a pass.
1267: 4. **Docs.** Update affected owner documentation, perform the no-comments check (remove unnecessary comments; retain necessary rationale), and prepare a complete PR description: intent, changes, verification commands/results, proof, risk and rollback. Record an explicit disposition if owner-doc changes are unnecessary; that does not skip the no-comments or description checks. `review_loop.docs` only controls extra reviewer rubric patterns, not this stage.
1268: 5. **Lint.** Run lint after docs so it covers documentation edits. Run the repository's workflow jobs locally where possible, preserving their test/lint ordering dependencies. Record unsupported jobs and environment/secret/event differences explicitly; local equivalence is not a claim that forge CI ran. Any unmet required local validation blocks rather than becoming an implicit pass.
1269: 6. **Exact-head publication barrier.** All local stages must qualify on one exact final commit `H`, not merely its ancestors. Any edit/commit during a later stage invalidates earlier local results; return through review -> test -> docs -> lint for the new head (a proved review carry is review-only, 25.8). Finish with a no-edit verification pass. Immediately before promotion, compare author, candidate and expected remote heads, current frozen-target tip and config binding. Moved author/candidate or stale evidence blocks promotion; an advanced target returns to freshness and validation. After validation passes, the internal promotion fast-forwards the Task branch from `S` to `H`, pushes without force, creates or updates the PR/MR, records promotion, and fast-forwards the Worker Sandbox only if it is clean. PR metadata failure after push is retried idempotently without bypassing validation for later code. After promotion, `posse publish --refresh "<summary>"` with fresh `--verify`, `--proof` and `--risk` values, run from the Sandbox or the candidate checkout while the author head is still the promoted head and the target has not moved, rewrites only the Posse-owned PR/MR title and body span; without `--refresh` it reports the candidate as already promoted.
